1
00:00:00,029 --> 00:00:03,950
Open the department name menu and choose
Security and Permissions.

2
00:00:04,309 --> 00:00:07,039
The resulting Security and Permissions
page contains a

3
00:00:07,039 --> 00:00:09,100
table of individual permissions.

4
00:00:09,489 --> 00:00:14,069
Read the Permission, Note and Selection
columns together before changing a row.

5
00:00:14,479 --> 00:00:17,969
Group Only and Roles provide additional
scope where offered.

6
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:22,340
This lesson uses a fictional training
department so we can compare a saved

7
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:24,340
delegation with its original setting.

8
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:26,289
Find Who can Add Users.

9
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:29,210
Its current selection is Department
Admins.

10
00:00:29,679 --> 00:00:33,360
The note explains that department
administrators and the managing member

11
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:37,700
can add users by default, and that group
administrators can be allowed to add

12
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:39,900
users only to the group they administer.

13
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:42,850
Read that scope before delegating this
task.

14
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:46,859
A station or community-response team may
need local roster

15
00:00:46,859 --> 00:00:50,869
administration without receiving every
department-wide responsibility.

16
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:56,079
For the practice change, set Who can Add
Users to Department and Group Admins.

17
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:59,069
This control saves when its selection
changes.

18
00:00:59,529 --> 00:01:02,859
Reload the page and confirm that the same
selection returns.

19
00:01:03,290 --> 00:01:06,600
Who can Remove Users still shows
Department Admins.

20
00:01:06,979 --> 00:01:10,029
These are separate decisions: giving a
group administrator

21
00:01:10,029 --> 00:01:14,080
permission to add a member does not change
the remove-users selection.

22
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:17,650
No person is created or removed in this
exercise.

23
00:01:17,799 --> 00:01:21,319
Return Who can Add Users to Department
Admins when the

24
00:01:21,319 --> 00:01:23,189
practice comparison is complete.

25
00:01:23,669 --> 00:01:27,199
After another reload, the original
selection is visible again.

26
00:01:27,709 --> 00:01:32,699
Use this same readback habit when making
an intended departmental change: confirm

27
00:01:32,699 --> 00:01:34,710
the exact row and returned value.

28
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:38,880
Record who should own the task before
delegating it, and review

29
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:42,280
that decision when personnel or group
responsibilities change.

30
00:01:42,439 --> 00:01:44,929
Scroll to Who can Create Trainings.

31
00:01:45,259 --> 00:01:49,160
The starting selection is Department
Admins with No Roles beside it.

32
00:01:49,550 --> 00:01:54,189
Choose Department Admins and Select Roles,
then open Select roles.

33
00:01:54,620 --> 00:01:59,510
This training roster offers named choices
including Rescue Technician and Paramedic.

34
00:01:59,850 --> 00:02:03,619
Select Rescue Technician for the example
and read the resulting Rescue

35
00:02:03,619 --> 00:02:05,680
Technician tag beside the permission.

36
00:02:06,010 --> 00:02:09,549
This chooses a role for this particular
permission; it does not

37
00:02:09,549 --> 00:02:12,619
demonstrate changing a member’s role
assignment or promoting

38
00:02:12,649 --> 00:02:14,589
anyone to department administrator.

39
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:19,500
After the role-selection exercise, remove
the practice selection and return Who can

40
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:21,689
Create Trainings to Department Admins.

41
00:02:22,109 --> 00:02:25,150
The final view shows that mode and No
Roles again.

42
00:02:25,570 --> 00:02:29,530
Compare both pieces, because a permission
mode and its selected roles are

43
00:02:29,530 --> 00:02:31,429
separate parts of the configuration.

44
00:02:31,910 --> 00:02:34,480
Our demonstration restores the training
baseline.

45
00:02:34,879 --> 00:02:38,369
For a real training coordinator, retain
only the delegation your

46
00:02:38,369 --> 00:02:40,740
department has actually decided to use.

47
00:02:40,909 --> 00:02:45,130
The location rows separate Who can see the
Location of Personnel from

48
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:47,209
Who can see the Location of Units.

49
00:02:47,579 --> 00:02:49,900
Both pictured selections are Everyone.

50
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:54,650
The personnel-location note explains the
Group Only option for limiting group

51
00:02:54,650 --> 00:02:56,680
administrators and roles to a group.

52
00:02:57,130 --> 00:03:00,429
Read the row’s selection and scope
together rather than treating the

53
00:03:00,429 --> 00:03:02,429
checkbox as the entire permission.

54
00:03:02,810 --> 00:03:06,480
These controls address who may see
locations; this view does

55
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:09,959
not establish that a device is currently
reporting its position.

56
00:03:10,219 --> 00:03:13,229
Return to the note above the Security and
Permissions table.

57
00:03:13,669 --> 00:03:18,269
It says changes take effect on the next
login to the Resgrid web application.

58
00:03:18,739 --> 00:03:22,269
After an intended change, plan a normal
login and check with

59
00:03:22,269 --> 00:03:23,889
the affected authorized account.

60
00:03:24,330 --> 00:03:28,440
Our screenshots verify saved settings, not
that second-account test.

61
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:33,430
A security company, search-and-rescue
team, community paramedicine or mental

62
00:03:33,430 --> 00:03:38,299
health service, wildland contractor,
industrial response team, or fire

63
00:03:38,299 --> 00:03:42,189
and E M S department can use these
controls to match administration

64
00:03:42,189 --> 00:03:43,959
to actual responsibilities.

